Subject: phy: airoha: opt into the XR1710G retail RX K-flow

The XR1710G 5.1.1.12 retail firmware runs ten final lock measurements,
keeps the LPF resistor override enabled, and writes the Gen2 result
into PMA 0x174 as well as the Gen1/Gen2 reserve fields. Its x2 path
also enables the per-lane K-flow control and latches the results with
a pulse before cycling the CDR power. Match the TX1 multilane bit for
the same retail x2 mode (SerDes interface selections 2=0 and 3=0).

Use this sequence only on the XR1710G with the board opt-in. Keep
the existing PLL/SSC, host reset timing and link speed policy.

Reference: XR1710G 5.1.1.12 uncompressed kernel Image offsets
  Rx_PR_Fw_Pre_Cal 0x3698d0, final sample 0x369cd0..0x369d58,
  LPF exit 0x369d80..0x369db8, IDAC writeback 0x369df4..0x369e18;
  PCIe_G3_L0L1_init x2 K-flow 0x36c440..0x36c670 and CDR pulse
  0x36c250..0x36c30c; TX1 multilane 0x369ff4..0x36a000,
  0x36c020..0x36c034, 0x36c428..0x36c43c. The mode mapping is
  confirmed by mtk_pcie_probe 0x36f9dc..0x36fa4c (SCU PCIC=2).
